# Rust module layout

- `use` imports, then `const` and `type` aliases at the top of the module.
- Order items by call flow: callers before callees. Public API and entry points before private helpers.
- Keep each `struct`, `enum`, or `trait` immediately followed by its `impl` block(s). Do not group all type definitions before all impl blocks.
- Put `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` at the end.

Example:

```rust
const TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_millis(500);

pub struct Service { ... }

impl Service {
    pub fn run(&self) { self.worker.poll(); }
}

struct Worker { ... }

impl Worker {
    fn poll(&self) { helper(); }
}

fn helper() { ... }

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests { ... }
```
